@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Typed direct and interprocedural lock-order analysis

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #343A40
  FontColor #212529
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "Call nodes + LockKind\nAcquireRead · AcquireWrite · Release" as TYPED #DBE4FF
component "Resolved lock Variable\nDefinition / DefUse / Reference" as ID #FFF3BF
component "Per-process ordered skeleton\nlock events + resolved calls" as SKELETON #C3FAE8
component "Finite acquisition summaries\nown plus callee resources" as SUMMARY #E5DBFF
component "Held-lock stack\nrelease removes latest matching lock" as HELD #D3F9D8
component "Lock-order projection\nA -> B: B acquired while A held" as GRAPH #FFE8CC
component "Shared projection_sccs\nresource components" as SCC #FCC2D7
component "All internal edges Read->Read" as READ #F1F3F5
component "LockOrderCycle\nprocesses · resources · sites/ranges · call" as REPORT #FFE3E3

TYPED --> SKELETON
ID --> SKELETON
SKELETON --> SUMMARY : resolved call targets
SKELETON --> HELD : direct order
SUMMARY --> HELD : call while lock held
HELD --> GRAPH
GRAPH --> SCC
SCC --> READ : inspect modes
READ --> REPORT : at least one conflicting mode
READ --> READ : all shared reads\nsuppress

note bottom of SUMMARY
  Monotone finite union terminates over the process/resource universe.
end note

note bottom of REPORT
  Witnesses distinguish holder/acquirer processes and retain via_call when interprocedural.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| normalized lock semantics |
|<#FFF3BF>| stable resource identity |
|<#C3FAE8>| ordered process evidence |
|<#E5DBFF>| interprocedural may-acquire closure |
|<#D3F9D8>| held-state transfer |
|<#FFE8CC>| resource order graph |
|<#FCC2D7>| reused SCC engine |
|<#F1F3F5>| shared-read suppression |
|<#FFE3E3>| advisory conflicting cycle |
endlegend
@enduml
